  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "07d7c37b-4345-4721-9f70-4a8c8b935d53",
      "name": "Physical Experimentation",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Floors have thresholds. Rooms have awkward corners. Wireless connections fail. Batteries run down. People walk through the path you carefully planned.\n\nReal environments have an efficient way of exposing assumptions.\n\nThat is why Myomaton is built around physical experimentation rather than demonstrations that work only under ideal conditions.",
        "heading": "Reality is an excellent design review"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 60,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "1d8815d4-147a-4f27-8e2b-65ca703e024e",
      "name": "Principles",
      "type": "collection",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "items": [
          {
            "id": "principle-001",
            "text": "Practical robotics becomes much more interesting when ordinary hardware can participate.",
            "heading": "Affordable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-002",
            "text": "The system should be possible to inspect, explain, modify, and repair.",
            "heading": "Understandable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-003",
            "text": "Useful machines should not become disposable because one component or service disappears.",
            "heading": "Repairable"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-004",
            "text": "Core behavior and safety should remain close to the robot rather than depending unnecessarily on remote services.",
            "heading": "Local-first"
          },
          {
            "id": "principle-005",
            "text": "Cloud and AI services can add capability, but basic ownership and usefulness should not depend on continuing payments or Internet access.",
            "heading": "No mandatory cloud or subscription"
          }
        ],
        "heading": "What makes something Myomaton?",
        "itemSource": "inline"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "grid",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 50,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "columns": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "680318d0-a606-4d70-af92-1b5a69735ca6",
      "name": "Introduction",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Useful robots have to work in the physical world.\n\nSo we build things, run them, find out what fails, change them, and try again. Navigation, sensing, charging, mechanical design, software, and interaction all look a little different once the robot leaves the workbench.\n\nThe machines shown here are working experiments. The point is not to make every prototype look finished. The point is to learn what actually works.",
        "heading": "Build. Test. Learn. Repeat."
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "split-text-first",
      "version": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:30:06.758769+00:00",
      "sort_order": 20,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "6c763a29-4404-4fe7-be6f-ab60de3bfcbe",
      "name": "Hero",
      "type": "hero",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "What should a useful personal robot actually be?\n\nMyomaton explores practical robots that are affordable, understandable, repairable, and genuinely useful — machines people can adapt, maintain, and keep using on their own terms.",
        "eyebrow": "My Own Robot",
        "heading": "Myomaton",
        "actionId": "af558c75-18b1-44b5-9c79-d14a7a66e13f"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "default",
      "version": 2,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:30:06.758769+00:00",
      "sort_order": 0,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "7cb671bc-8d5b-423e-bd17-87922bd5f9b0",
      "name": "Ownership",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "A robot you can actually call your own.\n\nA useful personal robot should not stop being yours because a subscription expires, a cloud service disappears, or the manufacturer decides the hardware is finished.\n\nMyomaton explores robots that can be understood, repaired, modified, and kept useful over time. Cloud services and AI can add capability, but ownership should not depend on them.",
        "heading": "What does \"My Own Robot\" mean?"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 10,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {
        "anchor": "about"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9d7472fd-f453-4690-8596-fd3e57c9ddca",
      "name": "Robot Ecosystem",
      "type": "intro",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "A useful robot may not need to do everything.\n\nA household can make more sense as a small ecosystem: different robots with different capabilities, sharing information and helping one another where useful.\n\nMyomaton is exploring both the individual machines and the common system that lets simpler and more capable robots work together.",
        "heading": "More Than One Robot"
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "stack",
      "version": 1,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "sort_order": 40,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "a0afbe15-927b-46f6-bb2b-474523124934",
      "name": "Primary Call to Action",
      "type": "cta",
      "status": "active",
      "content": {
        "text": "Follow the builds, experiments, failures, fixes, and occasional moments when the robot actually does what we hoped it would.",
        "heading": "See what happens next."
      },
      "page_id": "fd7bdc57-c9b7-4274-b871-43cf2e9b09ee",
      "variant": "default",
      "version": 3,
      "metadata": {},
      "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:30:06.758769+00:00",
      "sort_order": 80,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-02T03:09:49.561431+00:00",
      "configuration": {}
    },
